# Generic header

Identify an independent service clearly without implying government affiliation.

## Use the shared identity contract

The [header component](header.html#identity-and-navigation-have-separate-responsibilities) owns optional household identity, home-link meaning and the native-shell boundary. This retained generic-header page supplies the focused variant. Add [service navigation](service-navigation.html) only when separate destinations are needed, without duplicating native sidebar or account behaviour.

## When to use

Use a compact identity header when a page belongs to a named household or business interface and does not need a long navigation menu. It gives users a stable route home and a recognisable context. Use the full [header](header.html) when the task needs navigation; use [service navigation](service-navigation.html) for a set of related destinations.

The official generic header is intended for government services outside GOV.UK. That eligibility does not apply to this independent project. We adapt the structural idea only, using an explicit household or business name, with an optional authorised image.

