## Behaviour and content

The identity link returns to the service’s genuine home page. Do not use it to refresh the current route, open a menu or launch a device action. A long service name wraps without compressing the artwork. If a logo is supplied, keep its aspect ratio and colours on a suitable neutral surface.

Do not include a crown, GOV.UK logotype, NHS logo or a government ownership statement. A plain text name is a valid identity; do not require a crest or logo. The same rule applies to standalone previews and error pages.

## Accessibility and testing

Give an informative identity image a concise alternative name. Use empty alt when it duplicates the adjacent name. The surrounding link must have a meaningful destination. Check contrast and focus on every palette, and verify that the header does not obscure the skip link at high zoom. A service name is supporting context; the content still needs its own main heading.

## Home Assistant boundary and source

The companion’s own branding adapter has a separate compatibility contract. These HTML examples do not replace native HA routing. The structural reference is [GOV.UK Generic header](https://design-system.service.gov.uk/components/generic-header/); household names are invented examples. Global shell personalisation remains a [design specification](../get-started/personalisation.html), not a setting added by this documentation.
